On 26 May, 03:08, Meddyan <Medd...@gmail.com> wrote:
> Yesterday I was playing a few wizards, and was thinking about what the
> best possible start-up inventory could be. Heres what I would go for
> if I could control the RNG (assuming a magic marker and blind fold as
> well):
>
> Blessed scrolls of charging, enchant armour, and genocide. EA can be
> read right off the bat for a small AC boost, charging can be used when
> the marker runs low, and genocide can be used either in a pant-
> shitting emergency or to wipe out your least favourtie species (if you
> run into trouble in the mines, you might do both with by genociding
> h!). Also, having knowledge of these scrolls is also handy for magic
> marker writing as well.
>
> For potions, I'd take 2 blessed gain abilities and 1 holy water. The
> boosts to Str and Con mean a handy extra 100 carry capacity, and will
> probably ensure hungerless casting if you were unfortunate to start
> with 16 or less Int. Starting with Holy water has obvious benefits
> too, you can start manufacturing more as soon as you grab a pick-axe,
> a few junk potions, and find a fountain. You could also start writing
> blessed enchant armours very early too.
>
> I'd take a spellbook of Identify, just because it is so damn useful,
> and the earlier you can cast it the better, although you may need a
> level 1/2 Divination spell to build it up first. That can be arranged
> as soon as you max your luck though.
>
> For rings, there are quite a lot of goods ones to choose from. I'd
> probably settle for Teleport Control (convience + emergency, once you
> find a nymph or too) and Free Action.
>
> Finally, a wand of death, for getting you out of almost any fight that
> has turned bad. A wand of cancellation might be handy too, mainly so
> you have knowledge of it (help prevent accidents), and lets you create
> holy water/blank scrolls as soon as you find the junk to blank.
>
> So, what would you choose?

* blessed +1 quarterstaff
* blessed +0 cloak of magic resistance

Standard.

* blessed ring of conflict
* blessed ring of teleport control

Conflict, TC and levitation are the rings I usually consider wish-
worthy. It's always nice to start with 2 free wishes and we can't
start with levitation so here we are. Conflict will help with any
tricky situation and an early castle-storming and we're going to want
it later anyway. Teleport control is just handy, now we can get
teleportitis without fear for a great escape mechanism and we can also
chow down on tengu with impunity.

Poison resistance is tempting for the paranoid, but not really
optimal.

* blessed spellbook of force bolt

Standard.

* blessed spellbook of Charm Monster

The most broken spell in the game. And we even start with skill in
Enchantment!

* 3 blessed potions of gain ability

See below.

* 2 blessed scroll of enchant armor
* 1 blessed scroll of charging

Scrolls don't matter too much actually as we're planning on maxing
luck and abusing our MM as soon as possible. We've gone for 2 blessed
enchant armor to provide some early game AC on an item we're probably
going to hang onto. Charging to save some charges later.

* blessed wand of death (0:8)

One of the best emergency wands. It also allows us to take out
shopkeepers very early on. Others worthy of consideration : fire (for
emergencies), teleport (for emergencies) and cancellation (for the
lazy).

* uncursed magic marker (0:99)

A fully charged marker is worth a bit more than one wish. Better than
a blindfold, that's for sure (we can't start with both). It decides
our gameplan - get the luckstone, max luck, abuse the hell out of the
MM.

* blessed tooled horn

Castle key and Elbereth that works on minotaurs. Neat.

Starting stats :

St: 13 Dx: 7 Co: 15 Int: 17 Wis: 15 Cha: 7

And on turn 4..

St: 15 Dx: 10 Co: 18 Int: 20 Wis: 18 Cha: 10

Now as we gain levels (which we will be doing as quickly as possible)
we will be gaining a lot of HP and PW. We also have huge HP and PW
regen, hungerless casting, the ability to read and cast nearly all
spells we find, great melee damage output and full carrying capacity.
Str and Wis will naturally be exercised to maximum pretty soon. Dex
and Cha are nearly meaningless.

I think having lategame stats early on is the biggest advantage
potions can confer. The extra gain at level-up tots up quite quickly.
3 blessed full healing was also tempting for a nice HP buffer against
early game stupidity.

Now, we descend through the mines ASAP, killing all the gnomes for
levels and using charm monster on anything actually threatening. We
can consider killing any shopkeepers we found in the dungeon or
minetown for some points of protection. Do minesend quickly and get
the luckstone (and maybe some books/potions). Come back to minetown
and convert the altar if necessary. Max luck, make holy water,
Magicbane, get crowned, abuse the hell out of the magic marker for
books and scrolls. Do skokoban (optional). Descend to the castle and
the /oW. Win.



